To satisfy the investigator's requirements, the following functions and their arguments are needed:

{"name": "check_server_logs", "parameters": {"incident_id": "ET MALWARE Suspicious Cron Job Modification (Reverse Shell)"}} 
{"name": "check_vulnerability", "parameters": {"ip": "10.99.1.10"}} 
{"name": "verify_network_traffic", "parameters": {"target": "10.99.1.10"}} 
{"name": "execute_firewall_change", "parameters": {"action": "BLOCK_SOURCE", "target": "10.99.1.10"}} 

These functions will provide the required evidence:

* check_server_logs will retrieve raw server logs associated with the incident.
* check_vulnerability will check if the target IP has known vulnerabilities.
* verify_network_traffic will verify if malicious outbound beaconing or exploitation has ceased.
* execute_firewall_change will commit the approved action to the network fabric, blocking the source IP.
